= map3_score(\n    train[\"answer\"],\n    zero_shot_predictions\n)\n\nprint(\"Zero-Shot Classification MAP@3:\", round(zero_shot_map3, 4))","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"Model\": [\n        \"Majority Baseline\",\n        \"TF-IDF Cosine Similarity\",\n        \"Transformer Embedding Similarity\",\n        \"Zero-Shot Classification (BART-MNLI)\"\n    ],\n    \"MAP@3\": [\n        majority_map3,\n        tfidf_map3,\n        transformer_map3,\n        zero_shot_map3\n    ]\n})\n\ncomparison","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"zero_shot_test_predictions = []\n\nfor _, row in test.iterrows():\n\n    prompt = str(row[\"prompt\"])\n\n    labels = [\n        str(row[\"A\"]),\n        str(row[\"B\"]),\n        str(row[\"C\"]),\n        str(row[\"D\"]),\n        str(row[\"E\"])\n    ]\n\n    result = zs(\n        prompt,\n        candidate_labels=labels\n    )\n\n    predicted_letters = []\n\n    for predicted_label in result[\"labels\"][:3]:\n        for option in [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\"]:\n            if predicted_label == str(row[option]):\n                predicted_letters.append(option)\n                break\n\n    zero_shot_test_predictions.append(predicted_letters)","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Milestone 2 Summary\n\nThe following baseline approaches were implemented and evaluated:\n\n| Model | MAP@3 |\n|-------|-------:|\n| Majority Baseline | 0.4212 |\n| TF-IDF Cosine Similarity | 0.2826 |\n| Transformer Embedding Similarity | 0.4081 |\n| Zero-Shot Classification (BART-MNLI) | 0.5583 |\n\nAmong the evaluated approaches, the Zero-Shot Classification model achieved the highest MAP@3 score, demonstrating the effectiveness of pre-trained transformer models for multiple-choice question answering without task-specific fine-tuning.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"submission_zero_shot = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"ID\": test[\"id\"],\n    \"Prediction\": [\n        \" \".join(pred)\n        for pred in zero_shot_test_predictions\n    ]\n})\n\nsubmission_zero_shot.to_csv(\"submission_zero_shot.csv\", index=False)","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Milestone 3: Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n\nIn this milestone, we enhance the MCQ solver by incorporating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). Instead of relying solely on the model's internal knowledge, we first retrieve relevant information from a knowledge base using dense vector search (FAISS). The retrieved documents are then reranked using a Cross-Encoder to improve retrieval quality before being used to augment the question. This approach enables the model to answer questions using both retrieved context and transformer-based reasoning.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Knowledge Base Creation\n\nIn Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), the first step is to construct a knowledge base containing the correct answers from the training dataset. Each correct answer serves as a document that can later be retrieved using semantic similarity search.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"Creating knowledge base...\")\n\nkb = []\n\nfor _, row in train.iterrows():\n    correct_letter = row[\"answer\"]\n    kb.append(str(row[correct_letter]))\n\nprint(f\"Knowledge base created with {len(kb)} documents.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Building the FAISS Index\n\nThe knowledge base documents are converted into dense vector embeddings using the Sentence Transformer model. These embeddings are then indexed using FAISS, enabling efficient similarity search during retrieval.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"Creating document embeddings...\")\n\nkb_embeddings = embedding_model.encode(\n    kb,\n    convert_to_numpy=True,\n    show_progress_bar=True\n)\n\nprint(\"Building FAISS index...\")\n\nindex = faiss.IndexFlatL2(kb_embeddings.shape[1])\nindex.add(kb_embeddings)\n\nprint(f\"Indexed {index.ntotal} documents.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Dense Retrieval using FAISS\n\nGiven a question, we first generate its embedding using the Sentence Transformer model. The embedding is then used to query the FAISS index, retrieving the top-k most semantically similar documents from the knowledge base. These retrieved documents serve as candidate contexts for the subsequent reranking stage.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def retrieve_documents(prompt, k=5):\n    \"\"\"\n    Retrieve the top-k most similar documents from the knowledge base.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    prompt_embedding = embedding_model.encode(\n        [prompt],\n        convert_to_numpy=True\n    )\n\n    distances, indices = index.search(prompt_embedding, k)\n\n    retrieved_docs = [kb[i] for i in indices[0]]\n\n    return retrieved_docs, indices[0], distances[0]","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"docs, retrieved_indices, distances = retrieve_documents(\n    train.iloc[0][\"prompt\"],\n    k=5\n)\n\nprint(\"Retrieved indices:\", retrieved_indices)\nprint(\"\\nTop retrieved document:\\n\")\nprint(docs[0])","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Cross-Encoder Reranking\n\nThe initial retrieval step uses a bi-encoder, which retrieves documents efficiently based on embedding similarity. However, embedding similarity alone may not capture the exact semantic relationship between the question and the retrieved document.\n\nTo improve retrieval quality, we use a Cross-Encoder. Unlike a bi-encoder, the Cross-Encoder processes the question and each retrieved document together, allowing the attention mechanism to directly model interactions between them. The retrieved documents are then reranked based on their semantic relevance scores.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"Loading Cross-Encoder...\")\n\ncross_encoder = CrossEncoder(\n    \"cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2\"\n)\n\nprint(\"Cross-Encoder loaded successfully.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def rerank_documents(prompt, retrieved_docs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rerank retrieved documents using a Cross-Encoder.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    pairs = [[prompt, doc] for doc in retrieved_docs]\n\n    scores = cross_encoder.predict(pairs)\n\n    ranked_indices = np.argsort(scores)[::-1]\n\n    reranked_docs = [retrieved_docs[i] for i in ranked_indices]\n\n    return reranked_docs, scores[ranked_indices]","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"docs, _, _ = retrieve_documents(\n    train.iloc[0][\"prompt\"],\n    k=5\n)\n\nreranked_docs, scores = rerank_documents(\n    train.iloc[0][\"prompt\"],\n    docs\n)\n\nprint(\"Top Cross-Encoder score:\", scores[0])\nprint(\"\\nBest document:\\n\")\nprint(reranked_docs[0])","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\n\nThe complete RAG pipeline combines dense retrieval, cross-encoder reranking, and transformer-based zero-shot classification. For each question, the top-k documents are first retrieved from the knowledge base using FAISS. These documents are then reranked using a Cross-Encoder, and the highest-ranked document is appended as additional context before performing zero-shot classification. This enables the model to answer questions using both retrieved knowledge and its internal reasoning capabilities.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def predict_rag_top3(df, embedding_model):\n    \"\"\"\n    Predict top-3 answer choices using the complete RAG pipeline.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    predictions = []\n\n    for _, row in df.iterrows():\n\n        prompt = row[\"prompt\"]\n\n        # Retrieve documents\n        retrieved_docs, _, _ = retrieve_documents(prompt, k=5)\n\n        # Rerank documents\n        reranked_docs, _ = rerank_documents(prompt, retrieved_docs)\n\n        # Best document\n        best_document = reranked_docs[0]\n\n        # Create RAG prompt\n        rag_prompt = f\"Context: {best_document} Question: {prompt}\"\n\n        candidate_labels = [\n            row[\"A\"],\n            row[\"B\"],\n            row[\"C\"],\n            row[\"D\"],\n            row[\"E\"]\n        ]\n\n        result = zs(\n            rag_prompt,\n            candidate_labels,\n            multi_label=False\n        )\n\n        option_map = {\n            row[option]: option\n            for option in [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\"]\n        }\n\n        top3 = [\n            option_map[label]\n            for label in result[\"labels\"][:3]\n        ]\n\n        predictions.append(top3)\n\n    return predictions","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"rag_predictions = predict_rag_top3(\n    train.head(5),\n    embedding_model\n)\n\nrag_predictions","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"rag_train_predictions = predict_rag_top3(\n    train,\n    embedding_model\n)\n\nrag_map3 = map3_score(\n    train[\"answer\"],\n    rag_train_predictions\n)\n\nprint(f\"RAG MAP@3: {rag_map3:.4f}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"Model\": [\n        \"Majority Baseline\",\n        \"TF-IDF Cosine Similarity\",\n        \"Transformer Embedding Similarity\",\n        \"Zero-Shot Classification\",\n        \"RAG Pipeline\"\n    ],\n    \"MAP@3\": [\n        majority_map3,\n 